      "content": "that sounds much better. a \"high-value proof-of-concept\" is exactly the kind of language i need. \n\ncan you actually write out the specific paragraph for the slide? i want it to be punchy. maybe something like: \"The pilot study demonstrated a highly significant trend toward efficacy, confirming a strong biological signal that validates our approach.\" \n\ndoes that sound okay? or should we make it even stronger to really drive home that the efficacy is there?",
